Description:
    Generate a UUID column migration. Detects your database adapter
    and emits production-safe migrations.

Adapters:
    postgresql  → native :uuid column, concurrent unique index
    mysql       → CHAR(36) (default) or BINARY(16)
    sqlite      → TEXT column with unique index
    cassandra   → CQL files under db/cql_migrate/
    mongoid     → Mongoid::Migration under db/mongo_migrate/
    dynamodb    → aws-sdk script under db/dynamodb_migrate/
    couchdb     → HTTP API script under db/couchdb_migrate/

Modes (--mode):
    add_column      Add a UUID column/attribute (default).
    new_table       Create a new table/collection/database with UUID.
    promote_to_pk   Migrate an integer primary key to UUID.
                    Relational adapters only (postgresql, mysql, sqlite).

Examples:
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --uuid-version=4
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --column=public_id
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --backfill
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --adapter=mysql --mysql-storage=binary16
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --mode=new_table
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --mode=new_table --as-pk
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --mode=new_table \
        --extra-columns name:string total:decimal status:string
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --mode=promote_to_pk
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --adapter=cassandra
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --adapter=mongoid
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --adapter=dynamodb
    bin/rails generate uid_attribute:migration Order --adapter=couchdb

Options:
    --mode=MODE                add_column | new_table | promote_to_pk
    --column=NAME              UUID column name (default: uid)
    --uuid-version=N           UUID version: 4 or 7 (default: 7)
    --backfill                 Companion backfill migration
                               (relational add_column only)
    --no-concurrent            Disable concurrent index creation (PostgreSQL)
    --adapter=ADAPTER          Force adapter
    --mysql-storage=STORAGE    MySQL UUID storage: char36 (default) or binary16
    --as-pk                    Use UUID column as primary key (new_table)
    --extra-columns=PAIRS      Extra columns for new_table mode
                               (e.g., name:string total:decimal)
